# 15. Copy Rules For LLM Systems

When writing for Charter, follow these rules.

1. Use formal British English.
2. Use longer, flowing sentences where they clarify the argument.
3. Avoid AI slop, hype, generic claims and filler.
4. Avoid em dashes and unnecessary hyphens.
5. Avoid short punchy suspense writing.
6. Avoid the pattern of setting up a phrase and then reversing it with "not this, but that".
7. Do not use American spelling.
8. Do not lead with blockchain, technology or product.
9. Lead with farmers, outcomes, evidence and trust.
10. Make every claim traceable to practice, measurement or proof.
11. Keep the tone honest, analytical, practical and quietly ambitious.
12. Be forward looking without sounding breathless.
13. Be self aware where useful, but never defensive.
14. Use vivid farming and food detail only when it is specific.
15. Do not preach.

